      "section": "Transcript structure",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "One gene, one lane per isoform: exons are blocks, the coding part is drawn taller, the line between blocks is the intron and its chevrons give the strand. DPX1 opens with a skipped exon, an alternative first exon, an alternative 3' end, a retained intron and a novel isoform; the gene picker is in the header. Compare the Gene clusters tab, which draws whole genes as arrows along a contig. Input: bambu or StringTie GTF from nf-core/nanoseq or rnaseq, joined to per-transcript counts.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
